@startuml
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Segoe UI
skinparam defaultFontSize 11
skinparam ArrowColor #0b7a75
skinparam ComponentBorderColor #0b7a75
skinparam DatabaseBorderColor #6b7280
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #f3f4f6
skinparam NoteBorderColor #9ca3af

title How code moves from the workstation to production, one environment at a time

state "local\nworking tree on the operator workstation" as LOCAL {
  state "build --env local\nreads the working tree as it stands" as BLOCAL
  state "deploy --env local\nreads build/<target_id>/ only" as DLOCAL
  BLOCAL --> DLOCAL
}

state "dev\nbranch: dev" as DEV {
  state "build --env dev\nworktree of origin/dev in a temp dir" as BDEV
  state "deploy --env dev\nreads build/<target_id>/ only" as DDEV
  BDEV --> DDEV
}

state "qa\nbranch: qa" as QA {
  state "build --env qa\nworktree of origin/qa in a temp dir" as BQA
  state "deploy --env qa\nreads build/<target_id>/ only" as DQA
  BQA --> DQA
}

state "prod\nbranch: main" as PROD {
  state "build --env prod\nworktree of origin/main in a temp dir" as BPROD
  state "deploy --env prod\nreads build/<target_id>/ only" as DPROD
  BPROD --> DPROD
}

[*] --> LOCAL

LOCAL --> DEV : promote --from local --to dev\nhuman authorizes and the answer is recorded\nstash stack emptied, git add -A, whole tree staged\ncommit_governance_driver runs every scan\ngit commit --allow-empty then git push origin dev

DEV --> QA : promote --from dev --to qa\nhuman authorizes and the answer is recorded\ngit push --force-with-lease\norigin/dev -> refs/heads/qa\nthe local working tree is never read

QA --> PROD : promote --from qa --to prod\nhuman authorizes and the answer is recorded\ngit push --force-with-lease\norigin/qa -> refs/heads/main\nthe local working tree is never read

note right of LOCAL
  Code is authored here and nowhere else.
  A local build reads the working tree because
  local is the only place where uncommitted work
  is a legitimate thing to run.
end note

note bottom of DEV
  Only these three pairs are accepted:
  (local,dev) (dev,qa) (qa,prod).
  Any other pair is refused, so an environment
  cannot receive code that skipped the one before it.
end note

note bottom of PROD
  Deploy refuses a stale build before it dispatches:
  the manifest's git_head_sha must equal current HEAD,
  manifest.env must equal --env, and manifest.build must
  equal frontEndAdmin.BuildVersions.latest.build.
  Nothing certifies what shipped except the build itself.
end note

@enduml
